    <briefdescription>
<para>Handle-class for a particular &quot;location&quot;. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>This value-type uniquely symbolises a register or stack location, allowing manipulation of locations without concern for where that location is. Practically, this allows us to treat the state of the machine at a particular point as an array of values, rather than a map of values. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
